WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.790
Not every hunt discovers active attackers, and that is acceptable.

00:00:03.790 --> 00:00:06.374
A successful hunt may uncover malicious activity,

00:00:06.374 --> 00:00:10.802
validate that a concern does not currently appear present, identify visibility gaps,

00:00:10.802 --> 00:00:13.016
improve documentation, or refine future hypotheses.

00:00:13.016 --> 00:00:15.230
Negative findings can still provide value.

00:00:15.230 --> 00:00:19.290
If the hunt was well scoped and the data was strong,

00:00:19.290 --> 00:00:25.194
the team may gain confidence that a specific behavior was not observed during the period reviewed.

00:00:25.194 --> 00:00:29.623
Findings from hunts can become SIEM correlation rules, EDR detections, playbooks, dashboards,

00:00:29.623 --> 00:00:31.837
enrichment logic, and analyst training materials.

00:00:31.837 --> 00:00:34.420
Hunting turns investigative learning into operational improvement.

00:00:34.420 --> 00:00:35.158
Over time,

00:00:35.158 --> 00:00:39.955
threat hunting strengthens the organization's ability to detect and respond to future attacks.

00:00:39.955 --> 00:00:45.860
It helps security teams learn from their own environment instead of relying only on generic assumptions.
